    "q-37908": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37908",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-6}{{x}^{2}+x+9}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-3 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+x+9\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-6\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-3x-6 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-3x-27}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $21.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-6}{{x}^{2}+x+9}=x-3+\\frac{21}{{x}^{2}+x+9}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
