    "q-105586": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105586",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the remainder when $3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-6x+2$ is divided by $3{x}^{2}-2x+1?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+3 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-6x+2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9{x}^{2}-7x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9{x}^{2}-6x+3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-x-1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
