    "q-322774": {
      "dom_id": "step-q322774",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Express $\\frac{12{x}^{3}-20x+96}{2{x}^{2}-3x+5}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{2{x}^{2}-3x+5},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the reminder of the division.$$\n\n| $12{x}^{3}-20x+96$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{2}-3x+5$ | __ |  |  | $2{x}^{2}-3x+5$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+9 \\\\  & 2{x}^{2}-3x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,12{x}^{3}+\\phantom{0}0{x}^{2}-20x+96\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{12{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}+30x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,18{x}^{2}-50x+96 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,18{x}^{2}-27x+45}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-23x+51\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $6x+9,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-23x+51.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12{x}^{3}-20x+96}{2{x}^{2}-3x+5}=6x+9+\\frac{(-23x+51)}{2{x}^{2}-3x+5}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
