      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the remainder when $4{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-35x+17$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-3x-10?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-3x-10\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-35x+17\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-40x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+5x+17 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}+3x+10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $4x-1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $2x+7.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
