    "q-325106": {
      "dom_id": "step-q325106",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "What is the quotient of $-2{x}^{4}+11{x}^{3}-17{x}^{2}+3x+3$ divided by $-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x+1?$\n\nThe quotient is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-3 \\\\  & -{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-2{x}^{4}+11{x}^{3}-17{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,-\\,2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}+x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+6x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}-5x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the quotient is $2x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-{x}^{2}-5x+6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
