    "q-105619": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105619",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "What is the quotient of $2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x+2$ divided by ${x}^{2}-x+3?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x+2\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}-x+3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $2{x}^{2}+1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
