      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "What is the remainder of $-8{x}^{4}+18{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-12x+8$ divided by $2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+x+5?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4x+3 \\\\  & 2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-8{x}^{4}+18{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}-12x+\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,-\\,8{x}^{4}+12{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-20x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+8x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+3x+15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-4x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $5x-7.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
