    "q-325144": {
      "dom_id": "step-q325144",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "What is the remainder of $-4{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}-9$ divided by ${x}^{2}-2x+3?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{3}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}-9=-4{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+0x-9\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}-8x-5 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-2x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-4{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-\\phantom{00}{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}0x-\\phantom{0}9\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\,-4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-8{x}^{3}+11{x}^{2}+0x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,8{x}^{3}+16{x}^{2}-24x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{2}+24x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-5{x}^{2}+10x-15}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,14x+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $-4{x}^{2}-8x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $14x+6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
