    "q-114524": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114524",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$\\frac{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{3}$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1={x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+2x\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & {x}^{2}-2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}+0{x}^{2}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+2x+0}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}+2x,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} \\\\ .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-114524-a",
