    "q-324442": {
      "dom_id": "step-q324442",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "What is the remainder of $-2{x}^{3}-8$ divided by $-{x}^{2}+2x-3?$\n\nThe remainder is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{3}-8=-2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-8\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+4 \\\\  & -{x}^{2}+2x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-\\phantom{0}8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-4{x}^{2}+6x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-4{x}^{2}+8x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,2x+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is $2x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-2x+4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
