    "q-114523": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114523",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "What is the remainder when $3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-1$ is divided by $3{x}^{2}+2x-1?$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$ term. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing term with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}-1=3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+0x-1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+2 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}+2x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,{\\,\\,3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\text{ }6{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}+4x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4x+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-4x+1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
